  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Thursday)\nIssued at 952 PM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nA reinforcing cold front will continue across the Mid-South\novernight, bringing cooler temperatures Friday into the upcoming\nweekend. Saturday's highs will be 5 to 10 degrees below normal,\nspanning the mid 50s to low 60s. The first instance of freezing\ntemperatures this season will occur Sunday morning north of I-40.\nThe latest NBM probabilities show a 50 to 60 percent chance of\ntemperatures reaching 32 degrees in this area. Below normal\ntemperatures will fade as we move into next week due to a\ndeveloping upper level low over Texas. This feature will bring\nsoutherly winds back to the Mid-South, increasing daily highs to\nthe mid 60s and low 70s.\n\nDespite long term guidance hinting at a few shortwave passes by\nthe middle of next week, no widespread rainfall is forecast. The\nmain reason behind this is lackluster moisture availability\nwithin the atmospheric column. For now, expect next week to\nfeature near-normal temperatures and dry conditions.",
